  "term": "chorda tympani",
  "definition": "The chorda tympani is a branch of the facial nerve that runs through the middle ear and exits through the petrotympanic fissure. It carries taste signals from the front two-thirds of the tongue and sends parasympathetic nerve fibers to the salivary glands.",
